[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Sweet as Honey]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.69]What was 'sweet as honey' and why? | 什么是“甜如蜂蜜”？为什么？
[00:16.04]In 1963 a Lancaster bomber crashed on Wallis Island, | 1963年，一架兰开斯特轰炸机在瓦利斯岛坠毁，
[00:22.41]a remote place in the South Pacific, a long way west of Samoa. | 那是南太平洋的一处偏僻之地，位于萨摩亚以西很远的地方。
[00:28.60]The plane wasn't too badly damaged, | 飞机损坏得并不严重，
[00:31.61]but over the years the crash was forgotten and the wreck remained undisturbed. | 但多年来这次坠毁被遗忘了，飞机残骸一直无人过问。
[00:38.58]Then in 1989, twenty-six years after the crash, the plane was accidentally rediscovered in an aerial survey of the island. | 后来在1989年，坠毁26年之后，飞机在一次对该岛的空中调查中被偶然重新发现。
[00:51.34]By this time, a Lancaster bomber in reasonable condition was rare and worth rescuing. | 到这时，一架状况尚好的兰开斯特轰炸机已经很稀有，值得抢救。
[00:59.89]The French authorities had the plane packaged and moved in parts back to France. | 法国政府将飞机拆开包装，分批运回了法国。
[01:06.28]Now a group of enthusiasts are going to have the plane restored. | 现在一群热心人正准备修复这架飞机。
[01:11.64]It has four Rolls-Royce Merlin engines but the group will need to have only three of them rebuilt. | 它有4台罗尔斯-罗伊斯的“默林”发动机，但这群人只需修复其中3台。
[01:20.44]Imagine their surprise and delight when they broke open the packing cases | 想象一下他们打开包装箱时
[01:26.63]and found that the fourth engine was sweet as honey--still in perfect condition. | 发现第4台发动机甜如蜂蜜般完好无损时的惊讶与欣喜吧。
[01:34.21]A colony of bees had turned the engine into a hive and it was totally preserved in beeswax! | 原来一群蜜蜂把发动机当成了蜂巢，它被蜂蜡整个封存了起来！
